# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUNDLED ASSETS (fonts + sound effects), embedded directly in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything the game needs visually/audibly ships inside this single .py file
# instead of depending on loose files sitting next to it (which is what broke
# the custom font and the custom sounds before: if this script - or the built
# .exe - ever runs from a folder that doesn't also contain "fonts"/"sounds"
# next to it, those assets silently went missing). Embedding the raw bytes as
# base64 and loading everything into memory at startup means the font and the
# sounds always work, regardless of where the game is launched from.
#
# - Fonts (Comfortaa, OFL-1.1 licensed, static Regular/Bold from
#   github.com/googlefonts/comfortaa) are registered into Windows via
# - Fonts (Comfortaa, OFL-1.1 licensed, static Regular/Bold from
#   github.com/googlefonts/comfortaa) are registered for this process only,
#   with no install and no admin rights, using the native mechanism for
#   whichever OS the game is running on: AddFontMemResourceEx on Windows,
#   fontconfig's FcConfigAppFontAddFile on Linux, and CoreText's
#   CTFontManagerRegisterFontsForURL on macOS. Tkinter can then address the
#   font simply as "Comfortaa" everywhere.
# - Sound effects (your recorded move/error/capture wavs, plus a handful of
#   synthesized tones for click/victory/special) are played through
#   pygame.mixer, which - unlike the old winsound module - works the same way
#   on Windows, Mac, and Linux, so a single build of this game can genuinely
#   ship cross-platform.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

